---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/seo/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, COOKIE_DOMAIN } from '../config';

// NOTE (internal, not rendered): this is a standard, conservative starting
// policy. Confirm the legal entity name, governing jurisdiction, data-processor
// list, and retention periods with counsel before relying on it.
const lastUpdated = 'November 2, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | GovHub"
  description="How GovHub collects, uses, and protects your data across its AI government proposal and compliance platform."
>
  <main class="container">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', url: '/privacy/' }]} />

    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <div class="gh-divider-ridge" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how GovHub ("GovHub," "we," "us") collects,
        uses, and protects information when you use our website and platform (the
        "Services"). By using the Services, you agree to the practices described
        here.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Account information</strong> you provide, such as name, work email, company, and role.</li>
        <li><strong>Content you upload,</strong> including solicitations, past-performance data, and proposal drafts.</li>
        <li><strong>Usage data,</strong> such as log and device information collected automatically when you use the Services, and the pages you visit on this site (see section 7).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
      <p>
        We use information to provide, operate, secure, and improve the Services;
        to draft and review your proposals at your direction; to communicate with
        you; and to comply with legal obligations. We do not use your uploaded
        proposal content to train AI models.
      </p>

      <h2>3. How we share information</h2>
      <p>
        We share information with service providers who process data on our behalf
        under appropriate confidentiality and security obligations, and where
        required by law. We do not sell your personal information.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain information for as long as your account is active or as needed to
        provide the Services, and thereafter as required for legitimate business or
        legal purposes. You may request deletion as described below.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We protect information using encryption in transit and at rest, access
        controls, and tenant isolation. See the <a href="/security/">security
        page</a> for details.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, export,
        or delete your personal information. To exercise these rights, contact us at
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use cookies and similar technologies to run the site and to understand
        which pages and campaigns bring people to GovHub. Our own cookies:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>gh_s</strong>: identifies your current visit; expires after 30 minutes without activity.</li>
        <li><strong>gh_ft</strong>: how you first found us (the referring site, campaign tags and first page); 90 days.</li>
        <li><strong>gh_lt</strong>: the campaign tags of your current visit; 30 minutes.</li>
        <li><strong>gh_lid</strong>: set only if you arrive through a personal link in an email from us (section 8); 90 days.</li>
        <li><strong>gh_optout</strong>: remembers that you turned analytics off (below); one year.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We also use PostHog and Google Analytics to measure how the site is used,
        and the Meta Pixel to measure our advertising. These providers set their
        own cookies. If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, we do
        not load the Meta Pixel and do not link your visits to our emails. You can
        also control cookies through your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Links in our emails</h2>
      <p>
        When we email you directly, for example when we reply to a message you sent
        us, a link to this site may include a reference number for your record in
        our email system. It is not your email address. If you open such a link, we
        keep the reference in the <strong>gh_lid</strong> cookie and attach it to
        your visits in our own analytics (PostHog), so we can see whether what we
        sent was useful and follow up sensibly. We remove the reference from the
        page address before any other analytics provider loads, so it is not
        shared with Google, Meta or anyone else.
      </p>
      <p>
        To stop this, turn analytics off on this browser below, or email
        {' '}<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> and we will
        delete the link between your visits and your record.
      </p>

      <div class="optout" id="analytics-optout">
        <p class="optout-status" data-optout-status>Analytics are on for this browser.</p>
        <button type="button" class="optout-btn" data-optout-toggle>Turn off analytics on this browser</button>
        <p class="optout-note">
          This stops Google Analytics, PostHog and the Meta Pixel on this site,
          and removes the gh_lid email link. It applies to this browser only and
          lasts a year, or until you clear your cookies.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>9. Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>The Services are not directed to children and we do not knowingly collect data from them.</p>

      <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be
        reflected by the "Last updated" date above.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy? Email
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<script is:inline define:vars={{ cookieDomain: COOKIE_DOMAIN }}>
  /* The opt-out button. The gh_optout cookie is the record: LeadLink.astro
     reads it first in <head> on every page and switches off GA4, PostHog, the
     Meta Pixel and the gh_lid email link. This only also stops the page that
     is already open. */
  (function () {
    var box = document.getElementById('analytics-optout');
    if (!box) return;
    var status = box.querySelector('[data-optout-status]');
    var btn = box.querySelector('[data-optout-toggle]');
    function setCookie(name, value, maxAge) {
      document.cookie = name + '=' + value + '; Domain=' + cookieDomain + '; Path=/; Max-Age=' + maxAge +
        '; SameSite=Lax' + (location.protocol === 'https:' ? '; Secure' : '');
    }
    function isOut() { return /(?:^|; )gh_optout=1(?:;|$)/.test(document.cookie); }
    function render() {
      var out = isOut();
      status.textContent = out ? 'Analytics are off for this browser.' : 'Analytics are on for this browser.';
      btn.textContent = out ? 'Turn analytics back on' : 'Turn off analytics on this browser';
    }
    btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
      if (isOut()) {
        /* PostHog loads again on the next page and clears its own opt-out
           (Analytics.astro, loaded callback). */
        setCookie('gh_optout', '', 0);
      } else {
        setCookie('gh_optout', '1', 365 * 24 * 60 * 60);
        setCookie('gh_lid', '', 0);
        if (window.__ghGaId) window['ga-disable-' + window.__ghGaId] = true;
        if (window.posthog) {
          try { window.posthog.unregister('gh_lid'); window.posthog.opt_out_capturing(); } catch (e) { /* not loaded */ }
        }
      }
      render();
    });
    render();
  })();
</script>

<style>
  main { padding: 1rem 1.5rem 3rem; }
  .prose { max-width: 44rem; margin: 1rem 0; }
  .updated { color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  h2 { margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 1.25rem; }
  ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; color: var(--fg-muted); }
  li { margin: 0.4rem 0; }
  p { color: var(--fg-muted); }
  .optout {
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
  }
  .optout-status { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; color: var(--fg); font-weight: 600; }
  .optout-btn {
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.55rem 1.1rem;
    border-radius: var(--gh-radius-pill);
    border: 2px solid var(--gh-navy-600);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--gh-navy-600);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .optout-btn:hover { background: var(--gh-navy-600); color: #fff; }
  .optout-note { font-size: 0.9rem; margin: 0.75rem 0 0; }
</style>
